{
  "The texts the controls write, the locale their dates and numbers follow, and the direction: one `uiLocale` for the kit, with a pack per language loaded as it is asked for.": "",
  "Switching the language": "",
  "`uiLocale.use('tr')` loads the Turkish pack the first time, then every control on the page draws its texts and formats again. The Language menu in the header of these docs does the same.": "",
  "The page’s `<html lang>`, else the browser’s language. Set `lang` before the first control is made; `uiLocale.ready` settles once that language is in.": "",
  "Every text a control writes itself (a button’s name, a message, “No items”) comes from the pack of the language in use; English fills what the pack leaves out.": "",
  "Dates, numbers, the first day of the week and 12 or 24 hours follow `uiLocale.locale`; a control’s own `locale` prop wins for that control.": "",
  "`uiLocale.dir` is `rtl` for Arabic, Hebrew, Persian, Urdu…; the controls lay themselves out from `<html dir>`, which `@motifx-community/i18n` keeps in step.": "",
  "A change is one event, `onChanged`: the controls draw again on it, and so can your own texts. No binding reads `uiLocale`.": "",
  "A text with a count is an ICU message, `{count, plural, one {# record} other {# records}}`; a pack writes it the way its language counts.": "",
  "Packs": "",
  "Pack": "",
  "Where it comes from": "",
  "Built in. What a pack leaves out is shown in English.": "",
  "`uiLocale.use('tr')` loads it the first time, as a chunk of the package.": "",
  "The same packs as files, for an app that bundles or serves them its own way: `uiLocale.add('tr', pack)`.": "",
  "Where the kit asks for a pack it does not have: `(language) => fetch(`/i18n/ui/${language}.json`).then((r) => r.json())`. A language without a pack keeps the English texts.": "",
  "A pack of your own is a plain object of the kit’s texts: `uiLocale.add` gives a language its texts, `use` switches to it. A few texts are enough to start; the rest stay English until the pack has them.": "",
  "With your app’s translations": "",
  "An app translated with `@motifx-community/i18n` has one locale already. `connectI18n(i18n)` makes the kit follow it: when the app switches, the kit loads its own pack and switches too. The link is undone by what it returns.": "",
  "Your own texts that follow": "",
  "The kit follows nothing: a change of language is told once, through `uiLocale.onChanged`. Keep your own texts with it, and fill the kit’s own texts with `uiLocale.text`, plurals included.": "",
  "Formats of one control": "",
  "Dates and numbers follow the kit’s locale. A control given a `locale` of its own writes that one, whatever the kit’s language is.": "",
  "Checking a pack": "",
  "In the repository, `npm run locales` checks every pack the kit ships, and `npm run locales -- path/to/de.json` one of your own. The texts themselves are in `src/locales/en.json`; a pack is the same keys in another language.": "",
  "Check": "",
  "What it means": "",
  "A pack names every text of `en.json`; one it leaves out is shown in English, and the check says which.": "",
  "A key `en.json` does not have is a typo.": "",
  "A text fills the same `{values}` as the English one, in ICU; the plural forms are the language’s own.": "",
  "`UiStrings` and `en.json` name the same keys.": "",
  "Switches to `locale` (`tr`, `tr-TR`): its pack is loaded first when it is not there, then every control draws again. A later call wins over one still loading.": "",
  "The locale in use.": "",
  "The direction of the locale in use.": "",
  "The texts in use. Assigning a set changes the texts and keeps the locale: `uiLocale.strings = { ...uiLocale.strings, close: 'Shut' }`.": "",
  "A text of the kit with its values filled in: `uiLocale.text('gridRecords', { count: 3 })`.": "",
  "Adds the pack of a language, or more texts to it; a language in use shows them at once.": "",
  "Where packs come from; the package by default.": "",
  "Settles once the starting language is in.": "",
  "Raised once the language changed, with `locale` and `previous`.": "",
  "Keeps the kit’s language with your app’s translations (`@motifx-community/i18n`, or anything with `locale` and `onLocaleChanged`); returns what stops it.": ""
}
